.IP \fB\-fstrict\-aliasing\fR 4
.IX Item "-fstrict-aliasing"
允许the compiler to assume the strictest aliasing rules applicable to
正在编译的语言。对于 C（和 C++），这会激活基于表达式类型的
optimizations 基于 the type of expressions.  In particular, accessing
an object of one type via an expression of a 不同 type is not allowed,
除非 the types are \fIcompatible types\fR, differ only in signedness or
限定符，或者表达式具有字符类型。通过相应的向量类型访问标量
对象也是允许的。
.Sp
例如, an \f(CW\*(C`unsigned int\*(C'\fR can alias an \f(CW\*(C`int\*(C'\fR, but not a
\&\f(CW\*(C`void*\*(C'\fR or a \f(CW\*(C`double\*(C'\fR.  A character type may alias any other type.
.Sp
请特别注意如下代码：
.Sp
.Vb 4
\&        union a_union {
\&          int i;
\&          double d;
\&        };
\&        
\&        int f() {
\&          union a_union t;
\&          t.d = 3.0;
\&          return t.i;
\&        }
.Ve
.Sp
The practice of reading from a 不同 union member than the one most
最近写入的（称为"类型双关"）是常见的。即使启用
\&\fB\-fstrict\-aliasing\fR, type\-punning is allowed in C, provided the memory
is accessed 通过 the union type.  In ISO C++, type\-punning 通过 a union
类型是未定义行为，但 GCC 将其作为扩展支持。因此，上述代码
以上 works as expected.    However, this code might not:
.Sp
.Vb 7
\&        int f() {
\&          union a_union t;
\&          int* ip;
\&          t.d = 3.0;
\&          ip = &t.i;
\&          return *ip;
\&        }
.Ve
.Sp
类似地，通过获取地址、转换结果指针并解引用来访问具有未定义行为，
and dereferencing the result has undefined behavior, 即使 the cast
即使转换使用了联合类型，例如：
.Sp
.Vb 4
\&        int f() {
\&          double d = 3.0;
\&          return ((union a_union *) &d)\->i;
\&        }
.Ve
.Sp
The \fB\-fstrict\-aliasing\fR option 已启用 at levels
\&\fB\-O2\fR, \fB\-O3\fR, \fB\-Os\fR.
.IP \fB\-fipa\-strict\-aliasing\fR 4
.IX Item "-fipa-strict-aliasing"
控制 \fB\-fstrict\-aliasing\fR 的规则是否跨函数边界应用。
function boundaries.  请注意 if multiple functions gets inlined into a
单个函数时，内存访问不再被视为跨函数边界。
函数边界。
.Sp
